From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:38:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] nss-systemd: copy PASSWORD_SEE_SHADOW into the group record
 buffer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

nss_pack_group_record() left gr_passwd pointing at PASSWORD_SEE_SHADOW, which is part of the module's read-only .rodata. That breaks callers that modify the returned group before freeing it — in particular pam_modutil_cleanup_group() zeroes gr_passwd when the PAM handle is torn down, which segfaults on read-only memory.

Copy the placeholder into the caller-provided buffer, as nss_pack_user_record() already does.
---
 src/nss-systemd/userdb-glue.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nss-systemd/userdb-glue.c b/src/nss-systemd/userdb-glue.c
index 5bc89d5f9b..866c235908 100644
--- a/src/nss-systemd/userdb-glue.c
+++ b/src/nss-systemd/userdb-glue.c
@@ -229,6 +229,8 @@ int nss_pack_group_record(
         assert(g->group_name);
         required = strlen(g->group_name) + 1;
 
+        required += 2; /* strlen(PASSWORD_SEE_SHADOW) + 1 */
+
         STRV_FOREACH(m, g->members) {
                 required += sizeof(char*);  /* space for ptr array entry */
                 required += strlen(*m) + 1;
@@ -267,12 +269,13 @@ int nss_pack_group_record(
         array[n] = NULL;
 
         *gr = (struct group) {
-                .gr_name = strcpy(p, g->group_name),
                 .gr_gid = g->gid,
-                .gr_passwd = (char*) PASSWORD_SEE_SHADOW,
                 .gr_mem = array,
         };
 
+        gr->gr_name = stpcpy(p, g->group_name);
+        gr->gr_passwd = stpcpy(gr->gr_name, PASSWORD_SEE_SHADOW) + 1;
+
         return 0;
 }
 
